# PREDICTION for ROOT lane run 16, committed ALONE and BEFORE the run.
#
# STEP -1 of `scratch/lane-run-7-procedure.md`. The derivation is written out so it is
# checkable independently of whether the number matches — and that is not decorative: R19-06,
# R20-07 and D0A-R26-06 are three runs whose FIGURE was right and whose EXPLANATION was wrong,
# the last of them in THIS FILE. A matching number is not evidence the reasoning was sound.
#
# ORDERING IS CONVENTION, NOT MECHANISM (D0A-R22-01, reopened). `git log` on this file versus
# the result file is the only evidence the prediction came first. Held for runs 13, 14, 15.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY RUN 16 IS OWED
#
# Run 15 was clean and its freshness check was enforced. But it ran at `0ad6556`, BEFORE the
# round-27 remediation, and none of the following has executed at root:
#   * the ABSOLUTE frame deadline in `wire.rs` (D0A-R27-02) — a stalled or trickling peer
#     could hold the ROOT daemon before consent. Found on the first round that named the file.
#   * the AGGREGATE read budget replacing the per-object ceiling (D0A-R27-01), with the default
#     now COMPUTED as `PRE_CONSENT_BUDGET_BYTES / PEAK_MULTIPLE_OF_BUDGET`.
#   * `ceiling_from_var` rejecting a non-UTF-8 configured ceiling (D0A-R27-03).
#   * argv NUL validation at both doors.
#   * `consent_window_elapsed`, now the production expiry decision.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DERIVATION
#
# Base: run 15 measured EXECUTED 192 / SKIPPED 5 / reported 197 at root.
#       The current unprivileged pair is EXECUTED 180 / SKIPPED 25 / reported 205 (measured
#       2026-09-07 at b609ddf, re-measured by the pre-commit hook across all 17 targets).
#
# Delta since run 15: the round-27 remediation added EIGHT tests and removed none. One RENAME
# is not an addition (`boot_secs_reads_the_boottime_clock_...` ->
# `boot_secs_agrees_with_a_direct_boottime_read_and_reports_its_own_discriminating_power`).
# Each was checked for root-gating BY GREP of its body — geteuid, a SKIP branch, a
# bwrap_available guard, a path-existence branch:
#
#   canonicalize.rs  the_read_budget_is_spent_across_reads_not_reset_per_object    no gate
#   canonicalize.rs  the_derived_ceiling_admits_the_largest_executables_...        no gate
#   canonicalize.rs  a_non_utf8_configured_ceiling_is_refused_not_defaulted        no gate
#   canonicalize.rs  an_argv_entry_with_an_embedded_nul_is_refused_...             no gate
#   wire.rs          a_stalled_peer_cannot_hold_the_daemon_past_the_frame_deadline no gate
#   wire.rs          a_trickling_peer_cannot_extend_the_frame_deadline_...         no gate
#   wire.rs          a_complete_frame_within_the_deadline_is_still_accepted        no gate
#   store.rs         the_consent_window_decision_is_exact_at_its_edges             no gate
#
# ALL EIGHT UNGATED. Nothing here depends on euid, on a privileged facility, or on a file that
# root sees differently. The four canonicalize tests use a tempdir; the three wire tests use a
# `UnixStream::pair`; the store test is pure arithmetic.
#
# So:  192 + 8 = 200 EXECUTED.  The root skip set is UNCHANGED at 5:
#   b1_daemon_binary                      needs --features insecure-test-seams
#   an_unreadable_login_defs              this uid can read a 0000 file          (root-caused)
#   a_regular_login_user_is_not_refused   running as root                        (root-caused)
#   pidfd_refuses_a_recycled_pid_barrier  userns unavailable to root here        (root-caused)
#   live_logind_query                     standing DEFER
#
# CONSISTENCY CHECK, because both lanes must describe the SAME test set:
#   unprivileged  180 + 25 = 205 reported
#   root          200 +  5 = 205 reported
#
# **AND THIS TIME THE EQUALITY IS NOT THE EVIDENCE (D0A-R27-04).** Equal totals cannot detect a
# compensating removal and addition. Section 4b of the procedure compares `(target, test-name)`
# IDENTITIES as counters between the root log and unprivileged `--list`; that comparison is
# what the record must cite. A total of 205 on both sides is a necessary condition, not a proof.
#
# Root and unprivileged remain OVERLAPPING SETS, neither a superset: three of the five root
# skips execute unprivileged. 200 > 180 is NOT a coverage claim.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE TESTS WITH TIMING TOLERANCES — named in advance so a failure is DIAGNOSED, not re-run
#
# TWO of the eight are genuinely timing-dependent, both in `wire.rs`:
#   a_stalled_peer_...     400 ms deadline, asserts elapsed < 5 s   (12x margin)
#   a_trickling_peer_...   400 ms deadline, asserts elapsed < 5 s, with a writer thread
#                          feeding one byte per 40 ms
# The deadline is ABSOLUTE, so load makes it fire sooner rather than later — the margin is in
# the safe direction. A failure here is far more likely to be a real regression (a per-read
# timeout reintroduced, so progress buys time) than a slow machine. **Do not re-run to green.**
#
# Also carrying a tolerance, from run 15's list:
#   boot_secs_agrees_...   two clock reads within 1 s of each other
#
# **A METHOD NOTE, because it happened while writing this derivation.** The grep that classifies
# these flagged `the_consent_window_decision_is_exact_at_its_edges` as timing-dependent with 8
# matches. It is PURE — the matches were the substring `elapsed` inside the function name
# `consent_window_elapsed`. Same bare-word failure that made the decoration check miss
# `timeout` (D0A-R27, self-corrected). Verified by reading the body. **The greps in this
# protocol find candidates; reading decides.**
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT A GREEN RUN 16 WILL NOT ESTABLISH — carried because a residual kept beside the fix that
# created it is read as part of that fix
#
# 1. THE SUSPEND DIVERGENCE. Unmeasured, and now known to be worse than last recorded: a
#    reviewer's mutation swapped production CLOCK_BOOTTIME for CLOCK_MONOTONIC and the clock
#    test STILL PASSED, so on this lane it discriminates neither suspend behaviour nor clock
#    identity. The test now PRINTS `BOOTTIME - MONOTONIC` so the transcript states its own
#    discriminating power instead of a green implying it. **Expect that delta to read 0 on this
#    box, and expect the message saying it proves nothing about clock selection.** Expiry
#    coverage comes from `the_consent_window_decision_is_exact_at_its_edges`, which needs no
#    clock at all.
# 2. THE PENDING STORE HAS NO CAP. The read budget bounds ONE proposal; nothing bounds
#    accumulation. B1's one-action exit limits it within a single invocation and establishes
#    nothing about a B2 loop. Adjacent to what R26-04/R27-01 fixed, which is how it disappears.
# 3. THE 30 s READ DEADLINE, the 1 GiB pre-consent budget and the 8 GiB workstation floor are
#    engineering and deployment CHOICES, not demonstrated bounds. R27-01's defect was that the
#    implementation did not honour even the chosen budget; the budget itself is still
#    unvalidated.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A MISMATCH IS A RESULT. Record which side was wrong. Do not adjust this derivation until it
# agrees with the measurement.

EXPECTED_EXECUTED=200
EXPECTED_SKIPPED=5
EXPECTED_REPORTED=205
